From 1cde441b9370953996643939bc64e6aa01ddd864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:49:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp tr098] the shell's input contract in front of every
 native setter

Every SetParameterValues of the easycwmp product went through
common_set_value_check_param() (functions/common/common) BEFORE any
setter.  The C modules ported the setters, not that layer: the engine's
mparam_set_value calls the setter directly and the MTK platform hook
returned 0 at once for a native path.  So every writable parameter ported
to C in phases 1-5 accepted values the product refused -- among them the
characters of command injection, into UCI values that shell scripts read.

input_contract_mtk.c ports the layer once:
  - is_safe_input, line by line as grep sees `echo "$v"`: refuse when no
    line is printable ASCII, when any line is empty or blank (so ""), or
    when any line holds # ; & | < > ` $ \ ' ";
  - the check by the parameter's SHELL type: xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:int
    (busybox "[" number parsing), xsd:boolean (true/1/false/0),
    xsd:IPv4Address (a dotted quad anywhere, grep -o), xsd:IPv6Address
    (is_valid_ipv6).  xsd:dateTime is not emulated: its one writable
    parameter, PeriodicInformTime, is the engine's own.
shelltypes_mtk.h is GENERATED from the coverage matrix (gen-shell-types.py,
186 rows): the C DMLEAF type cannot stand in -- the shell checks only six
exact spellings ("xsd:Int" and "xsd:unsignedint" go unchecked) and checks
IPv4/IPv6 that C types as string.

dm_platform_param_method applies it at VALUECHECK, for native paths in the
compat build and for every path in the all-C build; paths still served by
the script keep the script's own copy.  Comments of P5b/P5c/P5d corrected:
"" and query-string URLs were never accepted, Timeout is range-checked,
Forwarding.Enable takes true/1/false/0 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
